      "message": "Figure I might as well just upload this for review -- let me know if this change isn\u0027t suitable.\n\nThe functionality of `gclient_paths.FindAllPossibleExecutables` is pretty much ripped wholesale from python\u0027s `shutil.which` (https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Lib/shutil.py#L1575). Unfortunately it doesn\u0027t natively support `which -a`-style behaviour, so we have to reimplement a bunch of it in order to return a list and not just the first one that matches.\n\nTested locally (Ubuntu 25.04), seems to work ok.\n\nChoosing Gavin to review because I *guess* there\u0027s a ga... @google.com on the original bug; fingers crossed it\u0027s the same person (external, so can\u0027t see full emails/names).",
